    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0581" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg567"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.20/632a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-06T00:00:00-04:00">May 6,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1445. The Combined Chiefs of Staff yesterday evening approved the War Department
                    recommendations for the BEF, including dates for movement of the first
                    contingents. This would be very soon.</p>
                <p>The War Department asks that we keep in mind that absolute secrecy of sailing
                    dates is essential to security.</p>
                <p>General Leitão de Carvalho<anchor n="56" xml:id="d529-f1"/> was the first to be
                    informed last night.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d529-f1" n="56" xml:id="d529-f1-content">
                <p>Senior Brazilian member of the Joint Brazil–United States Defense Commission.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
